From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 15:01:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Lazy @font-face loading: fetch only faces whose family is
 used

Eager fetching downloaded every declared @font-face source at
stylesheet-parse time. Real pages declare many faces that never
match an element (icon fonts, per-script subsets, alternate
weights behind unicode-range splits), so this multiplied both
network and resident decompressed-font cost by declared/used:
measured 12 fetches for 3 used families on a font-heavy
fixture.

Chrome's model: a face downloads only when font matching actually
needs it. This lands the coarse version (collect_font_faces
parses @font-face rules into PendingFontFace entries (queued
directly by add_stylesheet_for_node, or via the new
DocumentEvent::PendingFontFaces from the async nested-stylesheet
handler which holds no document borrow); after every style
resolve, flush_needed_font_faces fetches pending faces whose
lowercased family appears in some element's computed font-family
list. The used-family set is sticky, so late-declared faces for
known families fetch without a rescan, and the O(nodes) scan only
runs while unmatched faces remain pending. unicode-range
granularity (Chrome fetches per-range) is out of scope) family
granularity captures the dominant waste.

Post-fix: 3 fetches for 3 used of 12 declared.

Against blitz-dom 0.3.0-beta.3: NestedStylesheetHandler no longer
fetches faces itself, so its net_provider field goes.
